{{!
    @template core_course/coursecards (theme_saec override)

    UPTex/SAEC restyle of Moodle's card-grid wrapper. This exact template
    is real and load-bearing — it is used by:
      - course/templates/view-cards.mustache (the "My courses" page grid,
        linked from our sidebar's "Mis Cursos").
      - blocks/myoverview/templates/view-cards.mustache (the "Course
        overview" dashboard block).
      - admin/tool/moodlenet/templates/view-cards.mustache.

    Every one of those callers extends this template via Mustache's parent/
    block-override syntax and fills the classes block; core_course/coursecard.mustache
    (also overridden alongside this file) is included per-course and is
    itself extended by block_myoverview for $menu/$progress/$coursename/
    $coursecategory — none of that is touched here, only markup/classes on
    the grid wrapper. The .uptex-course-card visual rules live in
    scss/custom.scss (Fase 9 audit: promoted out of an inline style tag
    that used to live here).

    Example context (json):
    {
        "courses": [
            {
                "name": "Course 3",
                "viewurl": "https://moodlesite/course/view.php?id=2",
                "courseimage": "https://moodlesite/pluginfile/123/course/overviewfiles/123.jpg",
                "fullname": "Course 3",
                "hasprogress": true,
                "progress": 10,
                "visible": true
            }
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="card-grid mx-0 row row-cols-1 row-cols-sm-2 row-cols-lg-3 {{$classes}}{{/classes}}" data-region="card-deck" role="list">
{{#courses}}
    <div class="col d-flex px-0 mb-2">
        {{> core_course/coursecard }}
    </div>
{{/courses}}
</div>
